PCA:

1. Principle Component Analysis
2. No target so it is comes under unsupervised algorithm.
3. This can also be used in the preprocessing.
4. PCA converts the any number of column into a specific column
5. PCA can also be called "Dimensionality Reduction Technique"
6. It converts highly co-related data into non-corelated data.
7. It can also used for visualization , when i want to project high dimension data into lower dimension


Note:
 a. When we have column which is similar and you can't choose any column because all the column
    looks same and fine. Then you should choose PCA.
 b. PCA wont be selecting the column, instead it creates a new column
 c. no of new column that we needed will be decided on n_components parameter

Flows of Working:

1. So PCA also needs data to be standarized.
2. it calculates the covariance matrix. (summary about the relationship about the data or variables or column)
    2.1 positive co-variance (1.0)
    2.2 Negative co-variance (-1.0)
    2.3 unrelated(0)
3. We will be calculating the distance(EigenValues, EigenVector)

